      <exercise number="25"><!-- #25 -->
        <statement>
          <p>
            The position of a particle is given by <m>\mathbf{s}(t)=\langle-5t^2+7t-9,-2t^3+3t^2+4t-5 \rangle</m> with <m>x(t)</m> and <m>y(t)</m> measured in meters and <m>t\geq 0</m> measured in seconds. Find the acceleration vector at the time when the velocity vector is <m>\langle -3,4 \rangle</m>.
          </p>
            <ol marker="(A)">
              <li>
                <p>
                  <m>\mathbf{a}=\langle -3,4 \rangle</m>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  <m>\mathbf{a}=\langle -5,-2 \rangle</m>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  <m>\mathbf{a}=\langle -10,-6 \rangle</m>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
